              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                About the Events
              </h3>

              <p>
                <strong>August</strong> is an on-foot ARDF
                hunt using a low-power (milliwatt) hidden
                transmitter, the &ldquo;fox.&rdquo; Participants
                use directional antennas and signal-strength
                techniques to locate it on foot through the park.
                These are great events for newcomers &mdash; no
                prior experience is needed.
              </p>

              <p>
                <strong>September</strong> steps up to a full
                regional mobile T-hunt in west Snohomish County.
                You will take signal bearings while driving
                south of Marysville and west of SR-9, then
                complete a short on-foot leg to the finish location,
                which is intentionally undisclosed.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                What Is Fox Hunting?
              </h3>
              <p>
                Amateur Radio Direction Finding (ARDF) is a radio
                sport where participants use a directional antenna
                to locate a hidden transmitter. It combines RF
                skills, outdoor navigation, and teamwork. Any
                license class can participate, and loaner equipment
                (handheld radio and tape-measure Yagi antenna) will
                be available at every event.
              </p>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;">
                How to Get Involved
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Show up and hunt</strong> &mdash;
                  mentors will be present at every event, all
                  skill levels are welcome.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Borrow gear</strong> &mdash; handheld
                  transceivers and tape-measure Yagi antennas
                  available at each event; no equipment required
                  to attend.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Fill out the interest survey</strong>
                  &mdash; lets us plan loaner gear and mentoring:
                  <a href="https://forms.gle/LMkWH3sisKHKjaAJ9"
                     style="color:#1a3a5c;">
                    forms.gle/LMkWH3sisKHKjaAJ9
                  </a>
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  <strong>Spread the word</strong> &mdash; invite
                  a friend; new faces are always welcome.
                </li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                Reminder and day-before announcement emails are
